From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 01:01:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02223/11362] [outer-loop] E3: Carnot executable-world-model
 solver harness (induce->verify->refactor->plan)

After arXiv:2605.05138 (gpt-5.5 solves 15/25 ARC-AGI-3 games fully). The paper's
thesis IS Carnot's: the LLM is a PROPOSAL mechanism, the verifier is the moat.
- collect_transitions(): zero-quota offline (grid,action,data,next_grid) dataset at
  logical resolution (detect_cell downsample).
- WorldModelVerifier: THE grounding -- scores a codex-induced engine() against the
  real transitions, returns mismatch artifacts. Identity-baseline on ar25 = 35%
  (no-ops); a real engine must beat it.
- CodexProposer: codex/gpt-5.5 writes results/arc_e3/<game>/world_model.py (induce +
  refactor-toward-simpler / MDL proxy).
- plan_and_execute: BFS to is_level_complete INSIDE the verified model, execute in
  the real env, HALT on predicted!=observed divergence (the verifier-grounded safety).
Runner scripts/arc_e3_solve.py drives one game with bounded codex rounds. Live
validation on ar25 in flight.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
